"""The cards of Book 1, Cowl and the Buried Mansion, as data.

build_prompt_book.py turns them into
docs/art-production/cowl-prompt-book.html. Change a card here, rebuild, and
republish the page to the same link.

The creative lead's direction (11 November 2026):
- Cowl's run leans far forward, arms swept back (the ninja run).
- His jump looks cool.
- His idle sways and bobs; after chilling for a while he pulls out a blunt or
  a bong and smokes it.
- He starts with no weapon: a 1-2 punch and a kick.
- Top-tier, AAA animation. Later the same day: "too cartoony and not AAA top
  tier", so the standard is grounded and weighty (real body mechanics, no
  rubber limbs, no comic gags), painted to match the mansion mockups.
- His mockup is canon: bare hands, the beanie at its drawn length.
- World assets for the game as built (merged into main the same day): every
  piece the art pass in game/level/level_art.gd still draws as flat ink,
  sized to its 64-px tiles, plus the parallax, stairs, floors and the room
  plates repainted at full resolution.

A card's frames are (ticks, words) rows: ticks are sixtieths of a second at
60 fps. The builder checks that every animation card has one frame per cell.
"""

